      "metadata": {
        "name": "REINVENTING CITIES: ROMA TUFELLO",
        "author": "Isabell Siegelmayer, Alexander Rapp, Florian Rödel",
        "year": "2025",
        "tags": [
          "urbanism"
        ],
        "description": "second place<br>The transformation plan for the Tufello neighborhood adopts an interconnected, long-term strategy focused on increasing greenery and reducing sealed surfaces through phased milestones. The process balances technical interventions by officials with varying levels of resident participation, starting with communication and awareness before moving to tangible spatial implementations. The site, challenged by topography and infrastructure, is physically reimagined as four interconnected zones: a Cultural Cascade, community sports facilities, the civic-centered Campo Comune, and the newly reclaimed biodiversity-rich Parco Sor Romano. These new spaces are framed by a continuous network of diverse natural habitats, solidifying the overarching goal of ecological improvement and stronger civic engagement."
      }
